# Diary
The project diary lives at `docs/diary/{YYYY-MM}/{YYYY-MM-DD}.md`. It is the
project's narrative audit trail and is committed to git, separate from the
private memory store (see `41-memory.mdc`).

**Story branches:** the autonomous / implementer loop runs
`scripts/git/strip-narrative-logs-from-index.sh` before each commit so local
diary hook writes are **not** included in PRs (merge hygiene). Canonical diary
lines for shipped work still land on **`main`** at merge time or via follow-up
commits there; `.gitattributes` keeps `docs/diary/**` conflicts rare when merging
into `main`.

## When to author a summary
Write a real session/work summary into `.cursor/session-summary.md` when:
- a story is completed (after `STORY_COMPLETE`),
- a foundation document changed (brief, prd, architecture, tech-stack,
  constitution, ux*, design-system, environments, observability, test-strategy,
  or a new design under `docs/designs/`),
- a material decision was made,
- the session involved meaningful, multi-step work that future readers will
  want to reconstruct.

Skip it for trivial / single-tool turns — the diary should not narrate every
edit. Foundation-doc Write/Edit operations are auto-logged as one-line entries
by the same hook; do not duplicate those in the summary.

## What to write
Plain markdown, no front-matter. Cover:
- **What happened** — features built, bugs fixed, decisions made.
- **Outputs** — files created/changed, commits (short hash), tests, deployments.
- **Verification** — how you know it works (commands, results).
- **Next handoff** — open questions, follow-ups, blockers.

Keep it tight — paragraphs, not transcripts. Link instead of pasting; cite
files / commits / Linear ids.

## Heading convention
The hook owns the H2 section. Every entry starts with the timestamp on its
own H2 line — that's why the file always reads as a chronological log. **Do
not start your summary with `# Title` or `## Title`.** Use `### Section`
or below for internal structure; the hook automatically demotes any
`#`..`#####` headings in your summary by one level so the timestamp H2 stays
the unique top of each entry.

The materialised block looks like:

```
## 2026-04-26T07:30:00Z

_session-summary · persona <name> · branch <branch> · story <id>_

<your summary content, headings demoted by one level>
```

## How materialisation works
On every `stop` event, `.cursor/hooks/diary-append.sh`:
1. If `.cursor/session-summary.md` has non-whitespace content (after stripping
   any UTF-8 BOM), prepends an H2 timestamp header followed by an italic
   metadata line, demotes the summary's headings by one level, and appends
   the result to today's diary.
2. Truncates `.cursor/session-summary.md` so the next session starts fresh.
3. Exits silently when the source file is missing, empty, or whitespace-only.

The hook never writes a stub `[session-end]` line — if you want a record,
author one.
